WEBVTT

00:00:01.50 --> 00:00:06.65
This is journey thirty one of Hewn, the software factory: delete a project.

00:00:06.65 --> 00:00:09.89
Archiving hides a project and keeps everything.

00:00:09.89 --> 00:00:13.39
Sometimes an Owner wants Hewn's copy gone for good.

00:00:13.39 --> 00:00:16.48
This video shows an Owner deleting a project,

00:00:16.48 --> 00:00:20.40
and the repository it built staying exactly where it was.

00:00:21.55 --> 00:00:26.46
An Owner chooses Delete, types the project name exactly and confirms.

00:00:26.46 --> 00:00:31.43
Hewn's records, logs and stored artifacts for the project are removed,

00:00:31.43 --> 00:00:34.56
and the GitHub repository is left untouched.

00:00:34.56 --> 00:00:35.91
The dialog says so.

00:00:35.91 --> 00:00:41.53
Deleting a project with an active direction is refused with "Cancel the running

00:00:41.53 --> 00:00:42.74
direction first".

00:00:43.89 --> 00:00:45.94
Here an Owner opens Projects.

00:00:45.94 --> 00:00:49.48
Beside Archive, each of their rows now has Delete.

00:00:49.48 --> 00:00:53.94
Harbor CRM's direction was cancelled, so its Delete is enabled.

00:00:53.94 --> 00:00:59.95
The dialog asks the Owner to type the name, and says what goes: its directions, runs,

00:00:59.95 --> 00:01:02.50
decisions, events and spend history.

00:01:02.50 --> 00:01:07.88
Under the field it says the GitHub repository is kept; only Hewn's record is

00:01:07.88 --> 00:01:08.45
deleted.

00:01:08.45 --> 00:01:12.06
The Owner types only part of the name and moves on.

00:01:12.06 --> 00:01:17.51
The field says to type Harbor CRM exactly, and Delete project stays disabled.

00:01:17.51 --> 00:01:21.26
With the whole name typed, Delete project is enabled.

00:01:21.26 --> 00:01:22.61
The Owner confirms.

00:01:22.61 --> 00:01:26.36
In about a third of a second the row leaves the list,

00:01:26.36 --> 00:01:29.19
and a toast says the repository is kept.

00:01:29.54 --> 00:01:33.55
Hewn no longer knows the project: its page is not found.

00:01:33.55 --> 00:01:38.63
But the repository is still there on GitHub, with its README unchanged.

00:01:39.78 --> 00:01:42.48
Tidewater's direction is still running.

00:01:42.48 --> 00:01:47.73
Its Delete is disabled, and its name and tooltip say why: cancel the running

00:01:47.73 --> 00:01:48.84
direction first.

00:01:48.84 --> 00:01:50.63
Pressing it opens nothing.

00:01:50.63 --> 00:01:56.44
If the API refuses for any reason, the dialog says so, and that nothing was removed.

00:01:57.59 --> 00:02:01.00
The handler checks the same guard as Archive first,

00:02:01.00 --> 00:02:05.34
so a project with an active direction is refused with a conflict.

00:02:05.34 --> 00:02:09.35
Then it compares the typed name with the project's, exactly,

00:02:09.35 --> 00:02:11.02
so case and spaces count.

00:02:11.02 --> 00:02:14.76
A mismatch is a field error with the dialog's own words.

00:02:15.11 --> 00:02:18.55
Then it removes every row Hewn keeps for the project.

00:02:18.55 --> 00:02:23.41
That's the directions and their stages, runs, events, log lines, decisions,

00:02:23.41 --> 00:02:28.53
model calls, GitHub mutations, increments and their checks, and skills updates.

00:02:28.53 --> 00:02:32.23
All of it goes in one save, so a failure removes nothing.

00:02:32.23 --> 00:02:37.22
The design had planned a purge job, but these are small rows in one database.

00:02:37.22 --> 00:02:41.57
The new decision record explains why one save is simpler and safer.

00:02:41.57 --> 00:02:43.25
Nothing here calls GitHub.

00:02:43.60 --> 00:02:48.65
Once saved, every open Projects page hears that the project was deleted,

00:02:48.65 --> 00:02:49.92
and drops its row.

00:02:50.27 --> 00:02:54.66
The dialog enables Delete project only when the typed name matches.

00:02:54.66 --> 00:02:59.51
It shows the field error once the field is left with something else in it,

00:02:59.51 --> 00:03:01.15
as the invalid mock does.

00:03:01.50 --> 00:03:05.00
This sequence shows the whole path, from the row to the toast.

00:03:06.15 --> 00:03:09.09
The backend tests go through the real API.

00:03:09.09 --> 00:03:13.59
A project that ran its first stage, with a log line, a decision,

00:03:13.59 --> 00:03:16.25
a model call and a commit, is deleted.

00:03:16.25 --> 00:03:19.55
Afterwards every one of its tables counts zero.

00:03:19.55 --> 00:03:25.38
Another project's records are untouched, and the repository still holds its README.

00:03:25.38 --> 00:03:28.96
A name that differs is refused and deletes nothing.

00:03:28.96 --> 00:03:30.93
So does an active direction.

00:03:30.93 --> 00:03:35.63
A Viewer is forbidden, and a Projects page hears the deletion live.

00:03:35.63 --> 00:03:39.00
Before the endpoint existed, all of them failed.

00:03:39.00 --> 00:03:42.79
All three hundred and twenty seven backend tests pass.

00:03:43.14 --> 00:03:47.75
End to end, a behaviour test types part of the name, sees the error,

00:03:47.75 --> 00:03:49.58
types the rest and deletes.

00:03:49.58 --> 00:03:54.87
It then checks the project is gone and the repository's README is still there.

00:03:54.87 --> 00:03:59.89
Others cover Cancel, a failure and Try again, the refusal, and the Viewer.

00:03:59.89 --> 00:04:04.91
Against the old page the first test failed, with no Delete button to find.

00:04:04.91 --> 00:04:10.61
Visual tests compare the dialog's default, invalid, confirm, busy and failed states,

00:04:10.61 --> 00:04:13.46
and the Delete controls, with their mocks.

00:04:13.46 --> 00:04:18.95
An accessibility test checks each state, and that Escape returns focus to Delete.

00:04:20.10 --> 00:04:23.54
A failure keeps what was typed, so Try again works.

00:04:23.54 --> 00:04:29.00
The dialog reads the same in dark mode, and on a phone it becomes a bottom sheet.

00:04:30.15 --> 00:04:32.33
Journey thirty one is complete.

00:04:32.33 --> 00:04:35.91
Owners delete a project by typing its name exactly.

00:04:35.91 --> 00:04:40.48
Hewn's records go in one save, and the GitHub repository is kept.

00:04:40.48 --> 00:04:43.99
And a project with an active direction is refused,

00:04:43.99 --> 00:04:46.94
with "Cancel the running direction first".

00:04:46.94 --> 00:04:49.05
Next comes journey thirty two.
